     1	# Tool Input Validation
     2	
     3	| Field  | Value                |
     4	| ------ | -------------------- |
     5	| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
     6	| Status | In Progress          |
     7	
     8	Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
     9	
    10	## Validation at execute time
    11	
    12	- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a required-property rejection without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
    13	- A nested missing property is reported with its complete JSON Pointer path, including the containing object ([validated by: names the nested required property in a schema rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L31)).
    14	- A nested wrong-typed property is reported with its complete JSON Pointer path and expected type ([validated by: names the nested property path for a type rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L78)).
    15	- An enum rejection is reported with the failing property's JSON Pointer path ([validated by: names the property path when an enum constraint rejects input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L103)).
    16	- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: names the top-level property and expected type for a type rejection](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L57), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
    17	- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input and undeclared properties through unchanged once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L125)).
    18	- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
    19	
    20	## Schema compilation and caching
    21	
    22	- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
    23	- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses a static validator after the schema object changes](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L152)).
    24	- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.
    25	
    26	## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
    27	
    28	- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
    29	- A rejected tool call is visible to the provider as a `tool_result`, and a corrected retry can execute and complete the message without rejecting `processMessage` ([validated by: feeds a schema rejection back for a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L403)).
